        "VOCAB|||Story Flow|||Enhance your vocabulary with these essential terms and natural expressions:\n\n*   **Suddenly** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **Out of nowhere** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **Eventually** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **In the end** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **To make a long story short.** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n\n> 🗣️ **Pronunciation Tip:** Keep your vowels clean and practice saying these terms slowly.|||Elo: 'To make a long story short' is perfect when you realize you've been talking for too long.",
        "CONCEPT|||Setting the Scene|||Use the Past Continuous ('I was walking...') to set the background, and the Past Simple ('when I saw...') for the action.\n\n*   **Key Concept Explanation:** Understanding this rule allows you to sound natural and confident when speaking.\n*   **How it works:** Apply this structure directly in daily conversations.\n\n> 💡 **Tutor Pro-Tip:** Don't translate directly from Portuguese! Focus on the English chunk structure.|||Elo: Describe a background action you were doing yesterday when something interrupted you.",
