        "CONCEPT|||Will vs Going To (Review)|||Use 'Will' for spontaneous decisions or predictions. Use 'Going to' for planned actions.\n\n*   **Key Concept Explanation:** Understanding this rule allows you to sound natural and confident when speaking.\n*   **How it works:** Apply this structure directly in daily conversations.\n\n> 💡 **Tutor Pro-Tip:** Don't translate directly from Portuguese! Focus on the English chunk structure.|||Elo: If I drop my pen, will you say 'I will pick it up' or 'I am going to pick it up'?",
